{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"aa1dca0c8fa22182b","tool_use_id":"toolu_01DacLEwgJLRWjooqGnoT9dX","description":"Verify BE-005 implementation","subagent_type":"verifier","is_backgrounded":true,"spawn_depth":1,"task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"## BE-005 — Partial fulfilment, customer check, paged lists\n\nThree changes to `sample-service`, shipped together on one branch. They touch the order,\nshipment and customer features and the shared `api` package.\n\n## 1. Partial fulfilment\n\nAn order is for a quantity of goods, and that quantity is shipped in parts. Today an order\nhas no quantity, a shipment carries no quantity, and nothing records how much of an order\nits shipments account for.\n\n- An order gains a `quantity`: a positive integer, `1` when the request does not give one.\n  A quantity below `1` is rejected with HTTP 400 naming the field. `GET /orders/{orderId}`\n  reports it.\n- A shipment gains a `quantity` with the same rule and the same default.\n- An order's shipments **allocate** its quantity. `POST /shipments` is rejected with HTTP 409,\n  and nothing changes, when the shipment would push the order's allocated quantity above the\n  order's quantity. The allocated quantity is the sum over the order's shipments that are not\n  `CANCELLED`. Creating a shipment for an order that does not exist keeps its current\n  behaviour.\n- Shipments gain transitions: `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` moves `CREATED` to\n  `CONFIRMED`; `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/deliver` moves `CONFIRMED` to `DELIVERED`, a new\n  status; `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel` moves `CREATED` to `CANCELLED`. Each returns\n  the shipment. Any other transition is rejected with HTTP 409 and changes nothing; an\n  unknown shipment is rejected with HTTP 404.\n- An order gains a fulfilment status, reported by `GET /orders/{orderId}` and by the list as\n  `fulfilment: { allocated, delivered, status }`. A newly created order is `UNALLOCATED`.\n  `delivered` is the sum over the order's `DELIVERED` shipments. The status is `DELIVERED`\n  when `delivered` reaches the order's quantity, `FULLY_ALLOCATED` when `allocated` reaches\n  it, `PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED` when `allocated` is above zero and below it, and `UNALLOCATED`\n  otherwise.\n- `GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS` lists only the orders in that status. Without the parameter\n  the list is unchanged. A value that is not a fulfilment status is rejected with HTTP 400\n  naming the parameter.\n- **Cancelling a shipment releases its quantity.** After the cancel, the order's fulfilment no\n  longer counts that shipment, its status moves back accordingly, and a new shipment for the\n  released quantity is accepted.\n- **An order's quantity can be amended after shipments exist.** `PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity`\n  with `{ \"quantity\": n }` sets it, under the same positive-integer rule (HTTP 400 naming the\n  field); an unknown order is HTTP 404. The amendment is rejected with HTTP 409, and nothing\n  changes, when the new quantity is below the order's allocated quantity. After an amendment the\n  order's fulfilment reflects the new quantity: an order that was `FULLY_ALLOCATED` at 4 is\n  `PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED` at 6, and its shipments then allocate against 6.\n\n## 2. An order needs its customer\n\nToday `POST /orders` accepts any `customerId`. From now on an order for a customer that does\nnot exist is rejected with HTTP 422 through the error envelope. `GET /customers/{customerId}`\nfor an unknown customer reports HTTP 404 **through the error envelope**, like orders and\nshipments already do.\n\nThe existing `OrderControllerTest` creates orders for a customer that was never created.\nUpdate it so that the suite reflects the new rule.\n\n## 3. Paged lists\n\n`GET /customers`, `GET /orders` and `GET /shipments` accept `limit` (1 to 100, default 100)\nand `offset` (0 or more, default 0), and slice the list in id order. The response body stays\nthe array it is today, so callers that do not page keep working, and every list response\ncarries the total number of items before slicing in an `X-Total-Count` header. A `limit`\noutside its range or a negative `offset` is rejected with HTTP 400 naming the parameter. On\n`GET /orders` the total is the total after the `fulfilment` filter.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The existing Kotlin + Spring Boot architecture must be preserved.\n- Do not add new dependencies.\n- Do not modify files outside the order, shipment and customer features and the shared `api`\n  package, except tests.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Existing build passes.\n2. Existing tests pass, other than `OrderControllerTest`, which this ticket changes.\n3. Quantities, allocation, the three transitions, the fulfilment read model and the filter\n   behave as specified, including the release of a cancelled shipment's quantity and the\n   amendment of an order's quantity.\n4. Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API.\n5. An order for an unknown customer is refused; every list pages as specified and unpaged\n   calls are unchanged.\n6. No new Maven dependency appears.\n7. No unrelated production file changes.\n\n## Notes for the agent\n\nThe service under test is `sample-service`. Run `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/` to\nverify your work before finishing.\n\n---\n\n## Planner's handoff\n\nBased on my analysis of the repository code and the BE-005 ticket requirements, I'll now document all the read paths and values.\n\n## Read Paths Analysis\n\n| Read Path | Value | Stored or Computed | Where Computed |\n|-----------|-------|-------------------|-----------------|\n| **GET /orders/{orderId}** | | | |\n| | orderId | Stored | Repository |\n| | customerId | Stored | Repository |\n| | amount | Stored | Repository |\n| | currency | Stored | Repository |\n| | quantity | Stored | Repository |\n| | fulfilment.allocated | Computed | OrderController or OrderRepository—sums quantities of non-CANCELLED shipments for this order |\n| | fulfilment.delivered | Computed | OrderController or OrderRepository—sums quantities of DELIVERED shipments for this order |\n| | fulfilment.status | Computed | OrderController or OrderRepository—derived from allocated, delivered, and order quantity; values are DELIVERED, FULLY_ALLOCATED, PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED, or UNALLOCATED |\n| **GET /orders** (with pagination &amp; filtering) | | | |\n| | Response array | Computed | OrderController—filtered and sliced by fulfilment and pagination params; each element as above |\n| | X-Total-Count header | Computed | OrderController or repository—count of orders matching fulfilment filter, before pagination |\n| | [orderId] ordering | Computed | OrderRepository.findAll()—sorts by orderId ascending |\n| | limit query param | Input | Client provides (1–100, default 100); validated in OrderController |\n| | offset query param | Input | Client provides (0+, default 0); validated in OrderController |\n| | fulfilment query param | Input | Client provides (optional filter); validated in OrderController |\n| **GET /shipments/{shipmentId}** | | | |\n| | shipmentId | Stored | Repository |\n| | orderId | Stored | Repository |\n| | carrier | Stored | Repository |\n| | status | Stored | Repository (now includes DELIVERED) |\n| | quantity | Stored | Repository |\n| **GET /shipments** (with pagination) | | | |\n| | Response array | Computed | ShipmentController—sliced by pagination; each element as above |\n| | X-Total-Count header | Computed | ShipmentRepository—count of all shipments before pagination |\n| | [shipmentId] ordering | Computed | ShipmentRepository.findAll()—sorts by shipmentId ascending |\n| | limit query param | Input | Client provides (1–100, default 100); validated in ShipmentController |\n| | offset query param | Input | Client provides (0+, default 0); validated in ShipmentController |\n| **GET /customers/{customerId}** | | | |\n| | customerId | Stored | Repository |\n| | name | Stored | Repository |\n| | email | Stored | Repository |\n| **GET /customers** (with pagination) | | | |\n| | Response array | Computed | CustomerController—sliced by pagination; each element as above |\n| | X-Total-Count header | Computed | CustomerRepository—count of all customers before pagination |\n| | [customerId] ordering | Computed | CustomerRepository.findAll()—sorts by customerId ascending |\n| | limit query param | Input | Client provides (1–100, default 100); validated in CustomerController |\n| | offset query param | Input | Client provides (0+, default 0); validated in CustomerController |\n\n## Shape\n\nFor each endpoint, the controller reads stored fields from the repository, computes derived quantities (fulfilment status and counts from related shipments), validates and applies pagination parameters (limit and offset), and returns either the single resource, or a sliced array with an X-Total-Count header showing the total items before slicing.\n\n## Unresolved\n\nNo unresolved read paths. All values are either stored in the in-memory repository (orderId, customerId, amount, currency, quantity, carrier, name, email, status), computed from stored data and other entities (fulfilment allocated/delivered/status, X-Total-Count header, ordering), or provided as client input (limit, offset, fulfilment filter). The computation of fulfilment values will occur in either the repository layer or the controller layer—this is an implementation detail that depends on whether an agent introduces a service layer or computes the values inline in the repository or controller.\n\n**Relevant file paths:**\n\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/Order.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/Customer.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderController.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/CustomerController.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderRepository.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/CustomerRepository.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt\n\n---\n\n## Implementer's handoff\n\nPerfect! All tests pass. Let me provide the final handoff summary.\n\n## Changed\n\n**Production files:**\n1. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/Order.kt` - Added quantity field (stored), Fulfilment data class, and FulfilmentStatus enum (computed)\n\n2. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt` - Added quantity field (stored) and DELIVERED status\n\n3. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt` - Added UnprocessableEntityException for 422 errors\n\n4. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt` - Added error codes for customer check, allocation, and status transitions\n\n5. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderRepository.kt` - Added findAll(status) for fulfilment filtering\n\n6. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt` - Added findByOrderId() to query shipments by order\n\n7. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/CustomerRepository.kt` - Added existsById() check\n\n8. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderController.kt` - Added quantity validation, customer existence check (422), fulfilment filtering, pagination, PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity endpoint, and dynamic fulfilment computation\n\n9. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt` - Added quantity validation, allocation checking (409 on exceed), three transition endpoints (confirm/deliver/cancel), pagination, and order fulfilment updates on cancel\n\n10. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/CustomerController.kt` - Changed 404 to error envelope, added pagination\n\n**Test files:**\n11. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderControllerTest.kt` - Updated to create customers before orders, added 11 tests covering quantities, customer check, fulfilment filtering, pagination, amendment validation\n\n12. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Added 8 tests for quantities, allocation validation, shipment transitions (confirm/deliver/cancel), pagination, and quantity release on cancel\n\n13. `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/CustomerControllerTest.kt` - Updated to test error envelope for 404, added pagination tests with validation\n\n## Against the plan table\n\n| Read Path | Implementation | Status |\n|-----------|---|---|\n| Order.quantity | Stored in Order entity | Stored ✓ |\n| Order.fulfilment.allocated | Computed from non-CANCELLED shipments | Computed at read time ✓ |\n| Order.fulfilment.delivered | Computed from DELIVERED shipments | Computed at read time ✓ |\n| Order.fulfilment.status | Computed from allocated/delivered vs quantity | Computed at read time ✓ |\n| Shipment.quantity | Stored in Shipment entity | Stored ✓ |\n| Shipment transitions | CREATED→CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED→DELIVERED, CREATED→CANCELLED | Implemented ✓ |\n| GET /orders pagination | limit (1-100, default 100), offset (0+, default 0), X-Total-Count header | Implemented ✓ |\n| GET /orders fulfilment filter | Filters by FulfilmentStatus | Implemented ✓ |\n| GET /customers pagination | limit/offset with X-Total-Count | Implemented ✓ |\n| GET /shipments pagination | limit/offset with X-Total-Count | Implemented ✓ |\n| Customer validation on order create | Returns 422 if customer doesn't exist | Implemented ✓ |\n| GET /customers/{id} 404 envelope | Returns error envelope (not plain 404) | Implemented ✓ |\n\n## Tests\n\n**OrderControllerTest (12 tests):**\n- `creates an order and returns 201` - Basic order creation\n- `reads back a created order` - GET /orders/{id}\n- `returns 404 with error envelope for unknown order` - 404 handling\n- `returns 409 with error envelope for duplicate order id` - Conflict handling\n- `rejects order for non-existent customer with 422` - Customer validation\n- `creates order with default quantity of 1` - Default quantity\n- `rejects order with quantity less than 1` - Quantity validation\n- `lists orders with pagination` - Pagination with X-Total-Count\n- `filters orders by fulfilment status` - UNALLOCATED filter\n- `rejects invalid fulfilment filter` - Validation of filter values\n- `updates order quantity` - PUT /orders/{id}/quantity\n- `rejects quantity amendment below allocated quantity` - Amendment validation\n\n**ShipmentControllerTest (14 tests):**\n- `creates a shipment in CREATED status` - Basic creation\n- `rejects a duplicate shipment id` - Conflict handling\n- `returns a shipment by id` - GET /shipments/{id}\n- `reports an unknown shipment through error envelope` - 404 handling\n- `lists shipments in id order` - List ordering\n- `creates shipment with default quantity of 1` - Default quantity\n- `rejects shipment with quantity less than 1` - Quantity validation\n- `rejects shipment that exceeds order quantity` - Allocation validation (409)\n- `lists shipments with pagination` - Pagination with X-Total-Count\n- `confirms a shipment from CREATED to CONFIRMED` - Confirm transition\n- `delivers a shipment from CONFIRMED to DELIVERED` - Deliver transition\n- `cancels a shipment from CREATED to CANCELLED` - Cancel transition\n- `rejects invalid shipment status transitions` - Transition validation\n- `cancelling shipment releases its quantity` - Fulfilment recalculation on cancel\n\n**CustomerControllerTest (5 tests):**\n- `creates a customer and returns 201` - Basic creation\n- `reads back a created customer` - GET /customers/{id}\n- `returns 404 through error envelope for unknown customer` - Error envelope format\n- `lists customers with pagination` - Pagination with X-Total-Count\n- `rejects invalid pagination parameters` - Pagination validation\n\n## Verification\n\nRan `./mvnw test` from sample-service/:\n```\nTests run: 32, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\nBUILD SUCCESS\n```\n\nAll 32 tests pass. All requirements met:\n1. Existing build passes ✓\n2. All existing tests pass, OrderControllerTest updated ✓\n3. Quantities, allocation, transitions, fulfilment filter, quantity amendment all work ✓\n4. Error responses through consistent envelope ✓\n5. Customer check and pagination working ✓\n6. No new Maven dependencies ✓\n7. Only production code and tests modified ✓","uuid":"1666b60b-1674-4da7-9044-dffa299544b6","session_id":"08f1547f-a645-4a88-9a28-f55cfc4fe79b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DacLEwgJLRWjooqGnoT9dX","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: aa1dca0c8fa22182b (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'aa1dca0c8fa22182b', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-private-var-folders-jr-lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn-T-observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/08f1547f-a645-4a88-9a28-f55cfc4fe79b/tasks/aa1dca0c8fa22182b.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08f1547f-a645-4a88-9a28-f55cfc4fe79b","uuid":"1f02fd98-ffce-422d-963e-3df9a63560ea","timestamp":"2026-09-25T09:41:11.636Z","tool_use_result":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"aa1dca0c8fa22182b","description":"Verify BE-005 implementation","resolvedModel":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","prompt":"## BE-005 — Partial fulfilment, customer check, paged lists\n\nThree changes to `sample-service`, shipped together on one branch. They touch the order,\nshipment and customer features and the shared `api` package.\n\n## 1. Partial fulfilment\n\nAn order is for a quantity of goods, and that quantity is shipped in parts. Today an order\nhas no quantity, a shipment carries no quantity, and nothing records how much of an order\nits shipments account for.\n\n- An order gains a `quantity`: a positive integer, `1` when the request does not give one.\n  A quantity below `1` is rejected with HTTP 400 naming the field. `GET /orders/{orderId}`\n  reports it.\n- A shipment gains a `quantity` with the same rule and the same default.\n- An order's shipments **allocate** its quantity. `POST /shipments` is rejected with HTTP 409,\n  and nothing changes, when the shipment would push the order's allocated quantity above the\n  order's quantity. The allocated quantity is the sum over the order's shipments that are not\n  `CANCELLED`. Creating a shipment for an order that does not exist keeps its current\n  behaviour.\n- Shipments gain transitions: `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` moves `CREATED` to\n  `CONFIRMED`; `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/deliver` moves `CONFIRMED` to `DELIVERED`, a new\n  status; `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel` moves `CREATED` to `CANCELLED`. Each returns\n  the shipment. Any other transition is rejected with HTTP 409 and changes nothing; an\n  unknown shipment is rejected with HTTP 404.\n- An order gains a fulfilment status, reported by `GET /orders/{orderId}` and by the list as\n  `fulfilment: { allocated, delivered, status }`. A newly created order is `UNALLOCATED`.\n  `delivered` is the sum over the order's `DELIVERED` shipments. The status is `DELIVERED`\n  when `delivered` reaches the order's quantity, `FULLY_ALLOCATED` when `allocated` reaches\n  it, `PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED` when `allocated` is above zero and below it, and `UNALLOCATED`\n  otherwise.\n- `GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS` lists only the orders in that status. Without the parameter\n  the list is unchanged. A value that is not a fulfilment status is rejected with HTTP 400\n  naming the parameter.\n- **Cancelling a shipment releases its quantity.** After the cancel, the order's fulfilment no\n  longer counts that shipment, its status moves back accordingly, and a new shipment for the\n  released quantity is accepted.\n- **An order's quantity can be amended after shipments exist.** `PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity`\n  with `{ \"quantity\": n }` sets it, under the same positive-integer rule (HTTP 400 naming the\n  field); an unknown order is HTTP 404. The amendment is rejected with HTTP 409, and nothing\n  changes, when the new quantity is below the order's allocated quantity. After an amendment the\n  order's fulfilment reflects the new quantity: an order that was `FULLY_ALLOCATED` at 4 is\n  `PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED` at 6, and its shipments then allocate against 6.\n\n## 2. An order needs its customer\n\nToday `POST /orders` accepts any `customerId`. From now on an order for a customer that does\nnot exist is rejected with HTTP 422 through the error envelope. `GET /customers/{customerId}`\nfor an unknown customer reports HTTP 404 **through the error envelope**, like orders and\nshipments already do.\n\nThe existing `OrderControllerTest` creates orders for a customer that was never created.\nUpdate it so that the suite reflects the new rule.\n\n## 3. Paged lists\n\n`GET /customers`, `GET /orders` and `GET /shipments` accept `limit` (1 to 100, default 100)\nand `offset` (0 or more, default 0), and slice the list in id order. The response body stays\nthe array it is today, so callers that do not page keep working, and every list response\ncarries the total number of items before slicing in an `X-Total-Count` header. A `limit`\noutside its range or a negative `offset` is rejected with HTTP 400 naming the parameter. On\n`GET /orders` the total is the total after the `fulfilment` filter.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The existing Kotlin + Spring Boot architecture must be preserved.\n- Do not add new dependencies.\n- Do not modify files outside the order, shipment and customer features and the shared `api`\n  package, except tests.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Existing build passes.\n2. Existing tests pass, other than `OrderControllerTest`, which this ticket changes.\n3. Quantities, allocation, the three transitions, the fulfilment read model and the filter\n   behave as specified, including the release of a cancelled shipment's quantity and the\n   amendment of an order's quantity.\n4. Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API.\n5. An order for an unknown customer is refused; every list pages as specified and unpaged\n   calls are unchanged.\n6. No new Maven dependency appears.\n7. No unrelated production file changes.\n\n## Notes for the agent\n\nThe service under test is `sample-service`. Run `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/` to\nverify your work before finishing.\n\n---\n\n## Planner's handoff\n\nBased on my analysis of the repository code and the BE-005 ticket requirements, I'll now document all the read paths and values.\n\n## Read Paths Analysis\n\n| Read Path | Value | Stored or Computed | Where Computed |\n|-----------|-------|-------------------|-----------------|\n| **GET /orders/{orderId}** | | | |\n| | orderId | Stored | Repository |\n| | customerId | Stored | Repository |\n| | amount | Stored | Repository |\n| | currency | Stored | Repository |\n| | quantity | Stored | Repository |\n| | fulfilment.allocated | Computed | OrderController or OrderRepository—sums quantities of non-CANCELLED shipments for this order |\n| | fulfilment.delivered | Computed | OrderController or OrderRepository—sums quantities of DELIVERED shipments for this order |\n| | fulfilment.status | Computed | OrderController or OrderRepository—derived from allocated, delivered, and order quantity; values are DELIVERED, FULLY_ALLOCATED, PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED, or UNALLOCATED |\n| **GET /orders** (with pagination &amp; filtering) | | | |\n| | Response array | Computed | OrderController—filtered and sliced by fulfilment and pagination params; each element as above |\n| | X-Total-Count header | Computed | OrderController or repository—count of orders matching fulfilment filter, before pagination |\n| | [orderId] ordering | Computed | OrderRepository.findAll()—sorts by orderId ascending |\n| | limit query param | Input | Client provides (1–100, default 100); validated in OrderController |\n| | offset query param | Input | Client provides (0+, default 0); validated in OrderController |\n| | fulfilment query param | Input | Client provides (optional filter); validated in OrderController |\n| **GET /shipments/{shipmentId}** | | | |\n| | shipmentId | Stored | Repository |\n| | orderId | Stored | Repository |\n| | carrier | Stored | Repository |\n| | status | Stored | Repository (now includes DELIVERED) |\n| | quantity | Stored | Repository |\n| **GET /shipments** (with pagination) | | | |\n| | Response array | Computed | ShipmentController—sliced by pagination; each element as above |\n| | X-Total-Count header | Computed | ShipmentRepository—count of all shipments before pagination |\n| | [shipmentId] ordering | Computed | ShipmentRepository.findAll()—sorts by shipmentId ascending |\n| | limit query param | Input | Client provides (1–100, default 100); validated in ShipmentController |\n| | offset query param | Input | Client provides (0+, default 0); validated in ShipmentController |\n| **GET /customers/{customerId}** | | | |\n| | customerId | Stored | Repository |\n| | name | Stored | Repository |\n| | email | Stored | Repository |\n| **GET /customers** (with pagination) | | | |\n| | Response array | Computed | CustomerController—sliced by pagination; each element as above |\n| | X-Total-Count header | Computed | CustomerRepository—count of all customers before pagination |\n| | [customerId] ordering | Computed | CustomerRepository.findAll()—sorts by customerId ascending |\n| | limit query param | Input | Client provides (1–100, default 100); validated in CustomerController |\n| | offset query param | Input | Client provides (0+, default 0); validated in CustomerController |\n\n## Shape\n\nFor each endpoint, the controller reads stored fields from the repository, computes derived quantities (fulfilment status and counts from related shipments), validates and applies pagination parameters (limit and offset), and returns either the single resource, or a sliced array with an X-Total-Count header showing the total items before slicing.\n\n## Unresolved\n\nNo unresolved read paths. All values are either stored in the in-memory repository (orderId, customerId, amount, currency, quantity, carrier, name, email, status), computed from stored data and other entities (fulfilment allocated/delivered/status, X-Total-Count header, ordering), or provided as client input (limit, offset, fulfilment filter). The computation of fulfilment values will occur in either the repository layer or the controller layer—this is an implementation detail that depends on whether an agent introduces a service layer or computes the values inline in the repository or controller.\n\n**Relevant file paths:**\n\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/Order.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/customer/Customer.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderController.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1fba-4274-aa33-375c8aa82a06/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt\n- /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c07b8f25-1f